{"title":"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a cyclic quadrilateral. The side lengths of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> are distinct integers less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ebd842390a502751f429e3fbcc529e4f68816d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC\\cdot CD=AB\\cdot DA$\" width=\"167\" height=\"13\" />. What is the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/4/5442f300e3e2fd6d6516d361b218c3c01b19369c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\sqrt{\\dfrac{325}{2}} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\sqrt{185} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\sqrt{\\dfrac{389}{2}} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{\\dfrac{425}{2}} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\sqrt{\\dfrac{533}{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"542\" height=\"43\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80e67527934e0557de487e6fdc23ea439b269b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d5f81f182d0b2c07569dfc7ce37b85d901cabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c125ae5c4c453e15e1cca88cbcf5135549137f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = c$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2762ed3957f65b3d18cfb2dbd39bfc921d44ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = d$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" />.  We see that by the Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f75d6d58b03031bd7cb52a7ca886a8ddf369d21c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/86644a0d74ba9ba18fc2e69713901863ab6c3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle CBD$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/5/4b5749dfc23fa4e4ac3971c679cedd6879558dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD^2 = a^2 + d^2 - 2ad\\cos{\\angle BAD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"255\" height=\"16\" />.  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/9/0f9e2c1fd170f992e811de9f6a4ae97bcbee83ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD^2 = b^2 + c^2 - 2bc\\cos{\\angle BCD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"249\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1ea99f7d8c51a0673f220b40db1fdcb812408c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ad = bc$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral. As a property of cyclic quadrilaterals, opposite angles are supplementary so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38ad0a8b45f8fedb2acf4c5973bc3abc4f4f263.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD = 180 - \\angle BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"190\" height=\"16\" />, therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/2/a627037f9ba193fdc1c63afa38a9d9a98d5cff7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\angle BAD} = -\\cos{\\angle BCD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"212\" height=\"16\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e7076e3d013ee54a6fec0d3f36154f50c8ef407.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ad\\cos{\\angle BAD} = -2bc\\cos{\\angle BCD}$\" width=\"265\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Adding, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d2ea7a955e22a411510b848c9bee3ca561d8aa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2BD^2 = a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + d^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"201\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We now look at the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1ea99f7d8c51a0673f220b40db1fdcb812408c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ad = bc$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />.  Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/5/a75d29a3a31438e162d1b3050d3656c4863b4a2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />.  Then, we must have either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/c/e6c122a5f4ffcb58a92ffc845df880b199f6571c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />.  We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5cea31c66ebe6e26b3a41f6c64316f0f618b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = 6$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/e/2eeb57269daee143ec45dcedeadf422f2cf9b271.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />.  \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/3/793e6bfc94c650283ec9e18156dc60e0142f11d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2BD^2 = 196 + 49 + 36 + 144 = 425$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"279\" height=\"16\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40eda3b32803a0e4260c393662025208d23c0b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\sqrt{\\frac{425}{2}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"90\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As previous, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80e67527934e0557de487e6fdc23ea439b269b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = a$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/d/a7d5f81f182d0b2c07569dfc7ce37b85d901cabf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9c125ae5c4c453e15e1cca88cbcf5135549137f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = c$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/2/da2762ed3957f65b3d18cfb2dbd39bfc921d44ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = d$\" width=\"63\" height=\"13\" /> and proceed as above until the addition step. From here, note\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a741bb50a2087e68650d6ec9cce3474cd20430a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+d^2-b^2-c^2=4ad\\cos{\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"225\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/d/b5de3e66caee5b992b3690c126f173bd6f6bc69e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2ad\\cos{\\theta} = \\frac{1}{2}(a^2+d^2-b^2-c^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"252\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/4/914a828fd58c2237b499f86d5267b9dc704a4d74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+d^2-2ad\\cos{\\theta} = \\frac{1}{2}(a^2+b^2+c^2+d^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"331\" height=\"38\" />. Note that because of the bounds of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c72d3f209ec3895bcf546050ea1526fbb1aaf661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{\\theta}$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />, this is in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/8/6f8e050fdb42055aa8f902b5a4d065e7283c1865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-4ad, 4ad]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" />. We want to maximize this, so we pick the largest possible side length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d8e853f98b14d2a8363f651bdf6223193e21194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />. Then, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe4d6ebef2a09e428f2984fb2d677c342dbe1bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=7$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> to satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/f/48f321bf029f7fb84615b987e2aaebb96e2c1537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ad=bc$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />. We cannot pick <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because it is prime and the integers are distinct, so we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/49986ad1ae5d88da95d611165eb5055d9ffcaa25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/0/e608445fc9292541fffc8edb50c81748ebeca1b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=6$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />.This is the optimal set of side lengths that maximizes our expression, which comes out to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb9e85094d4a3bee9bd64dc1519b7112621368c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}(196+49+144+36) = \\frac{425}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"242\" height=\"38\" />. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/213cf75c75add1bff9211cd1a1c369cc8759b04f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />, so the answer is the square root of it, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40eda3b32803a0e4260c393662025208d23c0b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)} \\sqrt{\\frac{425}{2}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"90\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>- SumDumNerd\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B\">2010 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2010 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017222928\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.042 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.063 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 337/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8594/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.698      1 -total\n 58.81%    7.468      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 38.80%    4.927      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8834:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017222928 and revision id 286521. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}